'''Provence''' ({{Langx|bl|Provenza}}; {{Lang-are|Prouvènço}}; pronunciation: {{W|IPA|[pχoˈvã(n)sə]}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in northern [[Cerdanya]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It is bounded by the regions of [[Dríadas]] to the north and [[Pigüe]] to the east, and the [[Willi Mapu]] [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|indigenous nation]] to the south. 

The administrative seat of Provence is [[Santa Creu]] ({{Literal translation|holy cross}}), while the largest city is [[Rosario]]. Originally settled by [[Catharism|Catharist]] {{W|Catalan language|Catalan}} and {{W|Occitans|Occitan}}-speaking farmers fleeing persecution in {{W|France}}, Provence has historically been a primarily agrarian society. It is included in all definitions of [[Rural society in Balisca|Rural Balisca]].

